<h1>GCP billing export, FOCUS table in BigQuery</h1>
<p class="fine">gcp &middot; feeds <b>charges</b> &middot;
  <span class="chip st-in-progress">built</span>
  
  <span class="chip st-blocked">metered</span>
  
</p>


<section class="panel">
  <h2>What it costs to run</h2>
  <p>BigQuery on-demand querying is USD 6.25 per TiB scanned, first 1 TiB per month free, minimum 10 MB billed per table referenced. One monthly pull of a FOCUS table at this size is well inside the free tier; a dashboard that re-queries per page view is not. The reader takes a JSON dump from `bq query --format=json`, so the query is run once, deliberately, and never on a page render.</p>
  <p class="fine">The FOCUS export is Preview, hosted by Google in an immutable dataset with a 2-year TTL and no storage charge to you. Enabling it is Console-only: there is no gcloud command, REST endpoint or Terraform resource for the toggle. Backfill reaches the start of the previous month for multi-region datasets and nothing at all for single-region. Google omits several standard FOCUS columns and substitutes x_ ones.</p>
  <p class="fine">Authentication: service account with bigquery.dataViewer AND bigquery.jobUser.
    <a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/billing/docs/how-to/export-data-bigquery-tables/focus-export" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Provider documentation</a></p>
</section>




<section class="panel">
  <h2>How to get the file</h2>
  <ol class="rules"><li>In the Google Cloud console open Billing -&gt; Billing export -&gt; BigQuery export and enable the FOCUS export. There is no gcloud command for this toggle.</li><li>Run the query once from your own terminal, so the scan happens deliberately and you see what it costs.</li><li>Upload the resulting JSON file here.</li></ol>
  
  <p class="fine">If you would rather do it from a terminal:</p>
  <pre class="jd">bq query --format=json --use_legacy_sql=false --max_rows=200000 \
  &#34;SELECT ChargePeriodStart, ServiceName, ChargeCategory, BilledCost, &#34;\
  &#34;EffectiveCost, ConsumedQuantity, ConsumedUnit, SkuId &#34;\
  &#34;FROM \`PROJECT.gcp_billing_immutable_ACCOUNT_REGION.gcp_billing_export_focus_ACCOUNT\` &#34;\
  &#34;WHERE DATE(ChargePeriodStart) &gt;= DATE_SUB(CURRENT_DATE(), INTERVAL 60 DAY)&#34; \
  &gt; gcp-focus.json</pre>
  
</section>




<section class="panel">
  <h2>1. Give it the data - the short way</h2>
  <p class="fine">Drop the file straight in. A zip of the whole export folder is
  fine and is unpacked here; a single CSV or JSON is fine too. Nothing to type,
  no terminal, and it works the same whether it came from AWS, Azure, GCP or a
  cluster of your own. Up to 200 MB.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/connectors/gcp-focus-bigquery/upload" enctype="multipart/form-data"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<CSRF>">
